{"availability":"available","full":"sinnercode228/flowdesk-crm","name":"flowdesk-crm","description":"Full-stack mini-CRM & sales dashboard: Next.js, Fastify, Prisma, PostgreSQL, JWT+RBAC, deals kanban, analytics. Live demo runs in the browser.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-25T02:22:55Z","updated":"2026-10-09T09:13:32Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://sinnercode228.github.io/flowdesk-crm/","topics":["crm","fastify","jwt-auth","nextjs","postgresql","prisma","tailwindcss","typescript"],"demo":"https://sinnercode228.github.io/flowdesk-crm/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:43.919Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:43.919Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T07:01:43.919Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:01:43.919Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js","Node.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A small CRM for a sales team: a deal kanban, contacts, a deal drawer with notes and history, a dashboard, and two roles, admin and manager. A Next.js static export talks to a Fastify and Prisma API, and a shared package between them holds the zod contract, the permission policy and the analytics functions.","I built this as a demo on generated data; it is not a client product. The name FlowDesk is made up, and every company, contact and deal comes from a seeded generator in packages/shared/src/demo-data.ts: e-mails on .example domains, phone numbers in the reserved 555-01XX range.","Demo: runs the same REST API inside the browser, with its state in localStorage, so there is no server behind it. The login form comes prefilled with the admin account, and the Manager button fills in the other one (admin@flowdesk.example and manager@flowdesk.example, password demo1234 for both). The Reset data button in the header restores the original data."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sinnercode228/flowdesk-crm/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint